cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it as below."
title: KR-Housing-LongRAG-Bench
abstract: >-
  A copyright-safe Korean long-context benchmark for evaluating whether
  full-context LLMs can replace or complement RAG and table/tool pipelines over
  real housing announcements (입주자모집공고), public tabular data (MOLIT 실거래 /
  HUG 분양이력), and housing statutes. The public release contains QA labels,
  evidence locators, deterministic predicates, answerability labels, split and
  provider/region metadata, and long-context-bundle references — no raw source
  documents, no leaked answers, and no API keys. v0.9.4 keeps the 1,997 QA,
  questions, splits, gold fixes and evaluation scope of v0.9.3 (1,876 evaluated
  items: dev 1,534 / test_public 342). It adds verdicts for dense bge-m3
  retrieval with 50 passages on the 81 aggregation items for six models, run
  under a comparison rule fixed before any generation call, a gold-page recall
  rule that assigns each retrieved passage to one page (dev BM25 recall@5
  74.9%, test unchanged), and disclosures on the minimax-m3 reasoning flag and
  four July 2026 full-context re-calls. The release is not leaderboard-ready
  and has no sealed hidden split.
type: dataset
version: v0.9.4
date-released: 2026-10-12
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/comsa33/kr-housing-longrag-bench"
